License, v. 2.0. Copyright (c) 2026 schroeder247. SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0

The one package source, and every package id mapped to it (Learn, "Package Source Mapping"): a machine-level source
cannot supply a package the build restores, so no id can be substituted from another feed. nuget.org also holds the
released Community.Zabbix.* packages, which is where the package-validation baseline restores from (Directory.Build.targets).
-->
<configuration>
  <packageSources>
    <clear />
    <add key="nuget.org" value="https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json" protocolVersion="3" />
  </packageSources>
  <packageSourceMapping>
    <packageSource key="nuget.org">
      <package pattern="*" />
    </packageSource>
  </packageSourceMapping>
</configuration>
